WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.634
[ Chuckling ]

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.968
Get into these boots, y'all!

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:08.000
Get into these boots!

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.033
It's so good to be here.

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:11.734
I'm so happy to be back
in New York.

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:14.634
I moved last year
from Brooklyn to Georgia

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:16.434
to save the democracy.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:17.734
You're welcome.

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:19.367
[ Applause ]

00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:21.000
It was me.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.434
I usually say that
just to see who doesn't clap.

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:24.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:27.367
I'm sure they're here.

00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:29.601
I moved down there to vote
but also, obviously,

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:32.234
to get a gun,
because when in Rome...

00:00:32.234 --> 00:00:33.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:35.300
And by "Rome,"
I mean Rome, Georgia.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.100
You register to vote there,
it comes with a Smith &amp; Wesson.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.667
Oh, my goodness. I'm so happy.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:45.100
It's, like, weird because
the South is a true dichotomy.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.868
You know, I'm hard now.
I'm a gun owner.

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:49.334
But I'm also soft.
I say "good morning" to people.

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:52.100
-[ Laughter ]
-I'm a Jersey girl.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.167
We don't do that above
the Mason-Dixon line, okay?

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:57.901
I brought that back
up to New York City.

00:00:57.901 --> 00:00:59.801
People think
New Yorkers are tough.

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:01.868
You want to scare a New Yorker?

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:05.634
Smile, look them in the eyes,
and say, "Good morning."

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:08.534
Yeah, they will think
you about to rob them.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:11.000
Only thing worse is somebody
asked me for the time once.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.000
I said,
"I will mace you in your face.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:14.767
'What time is it?'

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.567
Where is your cellphone?"

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:18.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:23.167
If they laugh, I don't care.

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:24.701
[ Laughs ]

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:26.200
I actually miss things.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:27.534
I miss flying,

00:01:27.534 --> 00:01:30.334
which I never thought
in the pandemic I would miss.

00:01:30.334 --> 00:01:32.734
The last place I went
before everything went down

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:34.934
was to Burlington, Vermont.

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:36.934
I don't know
if anybody's ever been there,

00:01:36.934 --> 00:01:39.300
but let's just say there were
more Black Lives Matter signs

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.033
than Black lives.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.334 --> 00:01:45.267
-Yeah.
-[ Applause ]

00:01:45.267 --> 00:01:47.968
-It was a weird place.

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:50.567
I got off that plane. I said,
"Is this north of the wall?

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:52.834
What's happening right now?"

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:55.567
Perfect temperatures for
white walkers and ice cream.

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:59.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.467
I'm used to being the only
Black person somewhere,

00:02:01.467 --> 00:02:04.534
but on this flight to Vermont,
I was the only young person.

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:06.701
I thought it was
a flight to heaven.

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:08.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:13.934
They was old, old.
They wasn't regular old.

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:16.934
They sat me next to
a 90-year-old white lady.

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:18.934
Why do I know that?
Because she told me.

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.667
I didn't ask her a question.

00:02:20.667 --> 00:02:23.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.501 --> 00:02:25.400
I sat down.
She was like, "I'm 90."

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.501
I said, "I'm Black.
I don't know what's happening.

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:28.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:31.734
Why are we stating
our demographics?

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:34.868
Is this the Census?"

00:02:34.868 --> 00:02:37.067
She was a chatty 90.

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:39.200
I think she was trying
to get all her words out

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.767
before the end.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:42.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:46.501
Yeah, it was weird
'cause I don't usually talk

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:47.701
to people on airplanes.

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:50.133
I'm not a monster.
She was talking to me.

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:52.400
She was telling me stuff
I didn't ask.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.934
I was like,
"Yo, since we're talking,

00:02:53.934 --> 00:02:55.934
I didn't know
you could fly that old."

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:57.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.667 --> 00:02:59.534
Why we showing I.D.
at the airport

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:02.801
if anybody can get on the plane?

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:06.200
You not allowed to fly a certain
amount of pregnant, right?

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.901
That's on sight.

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:11.400
90? That's the end of
the third trimester of life.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:14.834
Why is she on the plane with me?

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:17.100
I'm not a doctor, Delta,
but death is crowning!

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.501
I see it!

00:03:18.501 --> 00:03:21.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.868
I know I sound ageist,

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:26.634
and that's probably
because I am, I think.

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:29.334
There's age minimums.
We need age maximums. Okay?

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:30.934
We need an age maximum

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:33.033
for flights, computer techs...

00:03:33.033 --> 00:03:34.467
presidents.

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:35.834
Um...

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:38.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:41.734
Right. Y'all agree. Y'all agree.

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:43.734
Get that motorcade on track.

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:45.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.267
[ Chuckles ]
And it was just so weird.

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:49.167
She just kept telling me stuff
I didn't ask,

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.200
letting me know she was
going to visit her big sister.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.601
She turned me into a owl.

00:03:52.601 --> 00:03:54.767
I said,
"WHO is your big sister?"

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:01.901
And last but not least,
she just, like, didn't know

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:04.234
how to talk to a young Black
person 'cause at one point --

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:06.300
I'm not making this up --

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:10.400
she just started naming
Black people she could remember.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.767
That got awkward real quick
'cause she 90.

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:15.634
She don't know no new Blacks.

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:17.767
She was hitting me
with throw-Blacks.

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:19.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:21.501
[ Applause ]

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:26.567
Yeah. Crazy.

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:28.200
We were talking about music,

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.467
and she was like,
"do you know Ella Fitzgerald?"

00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:33.067
First of all, how dare you?

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:35.834
Of course,
I know who Ella Fitzgerald is.

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:38.734
She was like, "Ella Fitzgerald
and Nat King Cole

00:04:38.734 --> 00:04:41.100
are my favorite singers."

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.167
And I wanted the conversation
to be awkward and end,

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:45.667
so I was like what can I say

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:48.601
to make her not want to talk
to me no more?

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:50.667
I was like, "Since we're
talking about favorites...

00:04:50.667 --> 00:04:52.634
you know Harriet Tubman?

00:04:54.534 --> 00:04:56.901
And Nat Turner.
They're my favorite slaves.

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:59.767
You don't want to talk anymore,
do you?"

00:04:59.767 --> 00:05:01.968
She was like, "No.
Moses is my favorite slave."

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:05.067
I was like,
"You know what? Um...

00:05:05.067 --> 00:05:07.968
Did you just out-slave me?
That is rude!"

00:05:07.968 --> 00:05:10.434
Moses was a great slave.
Top five.

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:12.801
My name is Joyelle. Thank you,
guys, for listening to me!

